NEARS-1612 AC1 — live proof that the back-press hint goes through NSnackBar
Device: emulator-5554 | worktree build feat/NEARS-1612-access-location (APK md5-matched, see below)

STATIC (re-verified by QA in the worktree, not merely reused)
  grep -cE '(^|[^a-zA-Z])SnackBar\('  access_location_screen.dart  -> 0   (no raw construction)
  grep -c  'ScaffoldMessenger'        access_location_screen.dart  -> 0
  grep -n  'SnackBar('               access_location_screen.dart  -> L539 only,
      inside showCustomSnackBar(...) = the AC6 out-of-zone toast, deliberately untouched.
      (NOTE: conductor reported this at L524; at HEAD in this worktree it is L539.)
  Diff at the back-press site replaces ScaffoldMessenger.of(context).showSnackBar(SnackBar(...))
  with:  NSnackBar.show(context, text: 'back_press_again_to_exit'.tr, status: NStatus.info);

LIVE (observed on device)
  On the Set Location screen, pressing the system Back key once produced the toast
  node in the accessibility tree:

      $ ui_list        # immediately after: adb shell input keyevent KEYCODE_BACK
      Back press again to exit

  'back_press_again_to_exit' is emitted from exactly one call site in this file, and that
  call site is NSnackBar.show(...). The hint therefore demonstrably routes through NSnackBar
  at runtime.

WHY THERE IS NO SCREENSHOT OF THE PILL (instrument limitation, not a defect of this change)
  NSnackBar.show internally presents via ScaffoldMessenger (nears_dls/lib/components/snackbar/
  n_snackbar.dart, NEARS-1390 GetX-free presenter), so the SnackBar is owned by the route's
  Scaffold. AccessLocationScreen's PopScope has canPop: true unconditionally and the callback
  ignores didPop (PRE-EXISTING, explicitly out of scope for NEARS-1612), so the route is torn
  down within ~200ms of the press and the pill is disposed with it.

  Five capture strategies were attempted and all lost the race:
    1. screencap at t+0.25s / t+0.4s / t+0.5s after the key event
    2. 6-frame host-side burst (adb exec-out screencap) immediately after the key event
    3. on-device chained `input keyevent; screencap` x4
    4. window/transition/animator_duration_scale set to 10x, capture at t+1.0s
       (scales verified reset to 1 afterwards)
    5. adb screenrecord (no ffmpeg / cv2 / imageio / av on host to extract frames)

  Reported honestly: AC1's criterion is demonstrated; AC1's screenshot instrument could not
  be run. See followups[].
